[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2282123169","pull_request_review_id":3127978665,"id":2282123169,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc6IBm-h","diff_hunk":"@@ -328,3 +328,10 @@ GH-108825\n Validate extension JSON: Error: Field 'classes/EditorExportPlatformExtension/methods/_get_option_icon/return_value': type changed value in new API, from \"ImageTexture\" to \"Texture2D\".\n \n Return type changed to allow returning both ImageTexture and SVGTexture. Compatibility method registered.\n+\n+\n+GH-109687\n+---------\n+Validate extension JSON: Error: Field 'builtin_classes/Vector2i/constructors/3/arguments': size changed value in new API, from 2 to 1.\n+\n+A new Vector2/Vector2i constructor was added to accept scalar values, there's no actual API change.","path":"misc/extension_api_validation/4.4-stable.expected","commit_id":"e98148b60d9a9322f05988d22e46befda20b0c5b","original_commit_id":"9d052fb36d1009dd6941e16d614e9a062de5905e","user":{"login":"Bromeon","id":708488,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwODQ4OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/708488?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon","html_url":"https://github.com/Bromeon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Yes, this **is** an actual API change, one which breaks GDExtension.\r\n\r\nThe way it works is that GDExtension fetches function pointers to the different constructors a builtin type provides. Here, likely the `Vector2i(int x, int y)` constructor. Now if I write an extension in Godot 4.4, fetching that constructor, and then someone loads my extension in Godot 4.6 (with changes from this PR), then the fetched pointer will actually point to the _new_ constructor taking only 1 argument. However, my code still relies on this being 2 arguments `x, y` and will call it accordingly.\r\n\r\nThis is a compatibility hazard that leads to undefined behavior. If at all, you'd need to list the new constructor last, so that existing indices aren't affected.","created_at":"2025-08-18T11:25:30Z","updated_at":"2025-08-18T11:25:31Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109687#discussion_r2282123169","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/109687","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2282123169"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109687#discussion_r2282123169"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/109687"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2282123169/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":333,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"original_line":337,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":10,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2282128026","pull_request_review_id":3127987083,"id":2282128026,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc6IBoKa","diff_hunk":"@@ -244,6 +244,8 @@ bool Variant::can_convert(Variant::Type p_type_from, Variant::Type p_type_to) {\n \t\t} break;\n \t\tcase VECTOR2: {\n \t\t\tstatic const Type valid[] = {\n+\t\t\t\tINT,\n+\t\t\t\tFLOAT,\n \t\t\t\tVECTOR2I,\n \t\t\t\tNIL,\n \t\t\t};","path":"core/variant/variant.cpp","commit_id":"e98148b60d9a9322f05988d22e46befda20b0c5b","original_commit_id":"9d052fb36d1009dd6941e16d614e9a062de5905e","user":{"login":"Bromeon","id":708488,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwODQ4OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/708488?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon","html_url":"https://github.com/Bromeon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"While this is not technically a compatibility breakage, I'm not sure if we would want this. It means you can now assign `1` to a `Vector2`, which significantly weakens type-safety and hides a lot of logic errors.\r\n\r\nI stand by my earlier opinion that this conversion should be as explicit as possible, at the cost of a few characters.","created_at":"2025-08-18T11:27:59Z","updated_at":"2025-08-18T11:31:42Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109687#discussion_r2282128026","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/109687","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2282128026"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109687#discussion_r2282128026"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/109687"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2282128026/reactions","total_count":5,"+1":4,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":245,"original_start_line":245,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":249,"original_line":251,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":8,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2282130047","pull_request_review_id":3127990843,"id":2282130047,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc6IBop_","diff_hunk":"@@ -328,3 +328,10 @@ GH-108825\n Validate extension JSON: Error: Field 'classes/EditorExportPlatformExtension/methods/_get_option_icon/return_value': type changed value in new API, from \"ImageTexture\" to \"Texture2D\".\n \n Return type changed to allow returning both ImageTexture and SVGTexture. Compatibility method registered.\n+\n+\n+GH-109687\n+---------\n+Validate extension JSON: Error: Field 'builtin_classes/Vector2i/constructors/3/arguments': size changed value in new API, from 2 to 1.\n+\n+A new Vector2/Vector2i constructor was added to accept scalar values, there's no actual API change.","path":"misc/extension_api_validation/4.4-stable.expected","commit_id":"e98148b60d9a9322f05988d22e46befda20b0c5b","original_commit_id":"9d052fb36d1009dd6941e16d614e9a062de5905e","user":{"login":"WhalesState","id":53877170,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzODc3MTcw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/53877170?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState","html_url":"https://github.com/WhalesState","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/